Article 1 (Purpose) The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters concerning the organization and staffing of the Secretariat established within the National Gambling Control Commission pursuant to Article 13 of the National Gambling Control Commission Act.

Article 2 (Secretariat) (1) There shall be one Secretary General in the Secretariat of the National Gambling Control Commission (hereafter referred to as the "NGCC"), and the Secretary General shall be appointed from among public officials in general service who belong to the Senior Executive Service.
  (2) The Secretary General shall, under the direction of the Chairperson of the NGCC, exercise overall control over the affairs under his or her jurisdiction, and direct and supervise the relevant public officials.

Article 3 (Subordinate organization) The Secretariat shall have the Planning and Coordination Division, the Prevention and Treatment Division, the Supervision and Guidance Division, the Investigation and Public Relations Division, and the Illegal Gambling Industry Monitoring and Reporting Center.

Article 4 (Division of Planning and General Affairs) (1) The Director of the Planning and Coordination Division shall be a Grade III or Grade IV public official. <Amended on Aug. 30, 2023>
  (2) The Director of the Planning and Coordination Division shall take charge of the following matters:
  1. Matters concerning the formulation and coordination of a comprehensive plan for the integrated management, supervision, and sound development of the gambling industry and for the eradication of illegal gambling activities;
  2. Matters concerning the enactment and amendment of statutes and regulations regarding the integrated management and supervision of the gambling industry;
  3. Matters concerning the integration of gambling industry sectors, or the application and adjustment of total volume caps on the number of business establishments, sales volume, etc. for individual gambling industry sectors
  4. Matters concerning the planning and coordination of the integrated management and supervision of the gambling industry;
  5. Support for the operation of the NGCC;
  6. Matters concerning consultation with, and support for, relevant organizations related to the gambling industry;
  7. Deleted; <Feb. 7, 2023>
  8. Matters concerning overall evaluation of the sound development of the gambling industry;
  9. Other matters not under the jurisdiction of other divisions or centers within the Secretariat.

Article 5 (Division of Prevention and Treatment) (1) The Director of the Prevention and Treatment Division shall be appointed from among Grade IV public officials. <Amended on Aug. 30, 2023>
  (2) The Director of the Prevention and Treatment Division shall take charge of the following matters: <Amended on Jun. 7, 2022; Feb. 7, 2023>
  1. Formulation and implementation of policies on the prevention and treatment of addiction;
  2. Matters concerning the calculation, imposition, collection, management, and operation of addiction prevention and treatment charges;
  3. Guidance and supervision of the Korea Problem Gambling Agency;
  4. Improvement of systems for the prevention and treatment of addiction, and support for corporations, organizations, etc. related to addiction prevention and treatment;
  5. Formulation and implementation of public relations plans for addiction prevention;
  6. Formulation of a comprehensive plan for investigation, survey and research, analysis, and evaluation of the current state of addiction;
  7. Matters concerning the development of integrated educational programs and the implementation of education to prevent addiction and the inducement of excessive gambling activities, etc.;
  8. Other matters necessary for the prevention and treatment of addiction.

Article 6 (Division of Supervisory) (1) The Director of the Supervisory Division shall be a Grade 4 public official. <Amended Aug. 30, 2023>
  (2) The Director of the Supervisory Division shall take charge of the following matters:
  1. Planning and overall control of on-site supervision of gambling business operators;
  2. Matters concerning institutional improvements regarding excessive gambling activities by gambling business operators;
  3. Matters concerning the verification and supervision of on-site conditions of gambling business operators;
  4. Verification and guidance regarding compliance by gambling business operators with applicable requirements;
  5. Matters concerning the guidance and supervision of advertisements and business practices of gambling business operators that unduly promote gambling;
  6. Matters concerning the handling of reports regarding excessive gambling activities, etc.;
  7. Other matters concerning the supervision of gambling business operators.

Article 7 (Division of Research and Public Relations) (1) The Director of the Research and Public Relations Division shall be appointed from among Grade IV public officials. <Amended on Aug. 30, 2023>
  (2) The Director of the Research and Public Relations Division shall take charge of the following matters:
  1. Formulation, coordination, and implementation of public relations plans for major policies on the gambling industry;
  2. Matters concerning investigation and research on the gambling industry as a whole;
  3. Production and management of statistics on the overall gambling industry;
  4. Research and analysis of the current status of the gambling industry and policy cases in major countries around the world;
  5. Establishment of an information infrastructure for the gambling industry;
  6. Support for the publication of a white paper on the gambling industry;
  7. Matters concerning exchanges and cooperation with institutions, organizations, etc. related to the gambling industry;
  8. Formulation and implementation of measures to change social perceptions of the gambling industry;
  9. Matters concerning support for media coverage and briefings.

Article 8 (Illegal Gambling Industry Monitoring and Reporting Center) (1) The Head of the Illegal Gambling Industry Monitoring and Reporting Center shall be a Superintendent. <Amended on Nov. 5, 2013>
  (2) The Head of the Illegal Gambling Industry Monitoring and Reporting Center shall take charge of the following matters:
  1. Matters concerning the monitoring, reporting, and request for investigation of illegal gambling industries;
  2. Matters concerning the receipt and processing of reports on illegal gambling industries;
  3. Matters concerning the monitoring of illegal gambling sites;
  4. Matters concerning cooperation with investigative agencies and other relevant institutions in relation to illegal gambling industries;
  5. Matters concerning the payment of rewards for reporting illegal gambling industries, etc.;
  6. Matters concerning research and public awareness campaigns for the prevention of illegal gambling industries;
  7. Other matters concerning the monitoring and reporting of illegal gambling industries.

Article 9 (Fixed number of public officials in the Secretariat) (1) The fixed number of public officials in the Secretariat shall be as specified in the Appendix.
  (2) The Chairperson shall determine the fixed number of public officials by rank within the Secretariat through directives, administrative rules, and other means. <Added on Apr. 11, 2023; Amended on Aug. 30, 2023>
  (3) Public officials assigned to the Secretariat shall be appointed from among public officials belonging to the Ministry of Culture, Sports and Tourism; provided, two of the fixed number of public officials (1 person in Grade IV and 1 person in Grade VI) shall be filled by public officials belonging to the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs; one person (1 person in Grade IV) by a public official belonging to the Ministry of Planning and Budget; and four persons (1 superintendent, 1 senior inspector, and 2 inspectors) may be filled by public officials belonging to the National Police Agency. <Amended Nov. 5, 2013; Apr. 11, 2023; Aug. 30, 2023; Feb. 25, 2025; Dec. 30, 2025>

